        {
         "@type": "meaningComprehension",
         "comprehends": [
          "copies/sz207mm8382.jsonld#inscription-text"
         ],
         "note": "Pencil, four figures on the lower (upright) panel, no other writing in the crop. Each figure is plain: a crossed 7, then 1, 2, 4, closed by a point. The separators are dropped, as reading.md describes, and the wider gap after the 7 groups them 7 | 124, so I read 7.1.24. The reservation is that the same four figures could be a roll number 7124 rather than a date; nothing else in the crop decides it, so the confidence is medium."
        }
       ]
      }
     }
    },
